B.LO=new A.c5("People all over the world celebrate Christmas, and every place has its own special traditions. Let us visit four countries!","world_map",null,B.X)
B.LM=new A.c5("In Mexico, families celebrate Las Posadas. For nine nights before Christmas, friends walk together in a procession, singing songs, and then have a party.","world_mexico",null,B.X)
B.LJ=new A.c5("At Mexican parties, children swing at a pi\xf1ata filled with treats. Red and green poinsettia flowers, which grow wild in Mexico, decorate many homes.","world_mexico",null,B.X)
B.LN=new A.c5("In Sweden, Saint Lucia Day is on December 13. A girl wears a white gown and a crown of candles, and the family eats sweet saffron buns.","world_sweden",null,B.X)
B.Mc=new A.c5("In Germany, towns hold Christmas markets with lights, music, sweets and gifts. Many families have Christmas trees and Advent calendars that count down the days.","world_germany",null,B.X)
B.M8=new A.c5("In the Philippines, people hang a parol, a star-shaped lantern, in their windows. Parols are made with bamboo and bright paper, and they glow at night.","world_philippines",null,B.X)
